    // ─── The fight's challenges ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    //
    // Fifteen opcodes in a row, kwh..kxb, all from the preparation phase except kwm and kwl, which
    // are from inside the fight. They are measured over 305 captures with the timeline of
    // BOTH directions together: pcap.streams separates by connection, and without merging them again by time
    // the real order is lost and one cannot see who answers whom.
    //
    // The complete dance:
    //
    //   kxa   S->C  how many have to be chosen; it arrives TWICE, before the kaa and after the kba
    //   kwo   C->S  panel setting         kwn  S->C  its confirmation, with the same value
    //   kwr   C->S  opening the selector (empty)
    //   kwx   S->C  THE LIST: { f1: 15, f2 repeated: ldd }, ALWAYS two candidates
    //   kwv   C->S  selecting one. The FIRST arrives on its own, 2-30 ms behind the kwx: it is the
    //               client's automatic preselection, NOT a click by the player
    //   kwi   C->S  hovering over a candidate. No answer, and the client keeps
    //               sending it during the fight, when nothing can be chosen any more
    //   kwj   C->S  validating   ->   kww  S->C  the challenge is FIXED
    //   kaq/kah     the ready; there the server sends the missing kww and fills in gaps
    //   kai         placement is over
    //   kwu   S->C  the final list, stuck to the jyy that starts the fight
    //
    // The challenge message that goes inside almost all of them is the ldd.

